 "tier1Summary": "Democrats swept the US [[e:2026 United States elections|midterms]], taking the House and at least 54 Senate seats. From January, [[p:Donald Trump]] faces a Congress that has promised to try to end the Iran war and the tariffs. Trump says he has no immediate plans to strike Iran, and Tehran says it can fast-track a plan to reopen Hormuz. Oil fell.\n\nAcross the hemisphere, Canada reports more intense trade talks, while Mexico missed its pre-vote deal. Washington met Venezuela's new foreign minister and reportedly backs a 2027 path toward elections. [[p:Flávio Bolsonaro]]'s exit to Miami via Argentina set off a row between Brasília and Buenos Aires. El Salvador's troop surge in Haiti grows.\n\nElsewhere, Israel's results leave both blocs short of a majority as Herzog consults, Ukraine–Russia talks are set for 10–11 Nov in Abu Dhabi, and Ethiopia expelled Sudanese diplomats.",
